<% content_for :title, "Your contractors need websites. I build them. You keep 30%. — cyberjosef" %>

<header class="header">
  <div class="page">
    <a class="wordmark" href="<%= root_path %>">cyberjosef</a>
    <div class="header-actions">
      <button type="button" class="theme-toggle" data-theme-toggle aria-label="Switch theme">
        <svg class="icon-moon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"
             stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M21 12.79A9 9 0 1 1 11.21 3 7 7 0 0 0 21 12.79z" />
        </svg>
        <svg class="icon-sun" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"
             stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4" />
          <path d="M12 2v2M12 20v2M4.93 4.93l1.41 1.41M17.66 17.66l1.41 1.41M2 12h2M20 12h2M6.34 17.66l-1.41 1.41M19.07 4.93l-1.41 1.41" />
        </svg>
      </button>
      <a class="btn btn--primary btn--sm" href="#start">Become a partner</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main>

  <section style="padding: 64px 0 8px">
    <div class="page">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div>
          <h1 class="display-xl" style="max-width:18ch">Your contractors need websites. I build them. You keep 30%.</h1>

          <p class="body muted" style="font-size:17px; line-height:1.5; max-width:46ch; margin:16px 0 28px">
            You teach plumbers, roofers, cleaners how to grow. Growth needs a site,
            reviews and booked jobs — that's what I sell. You recommend it once,
            I build, host and support everything. 30% of every invoice is yours.
            Every month, for as long as the client pays.
          </p>

          <div class="row gap-3">
            <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#start">Become a partner</a>
            <a class="btn btn--outline" href="#systems">See the systems</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-card-slot">
          <div class="access-card" data-tilt-card>
            <div class="access-card-bg"></div>
            <div class="access-card-edge"></div>

            <div class="access-card-head">
              <span class="mark" data-card-mark aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <p class="card-title">Trades partner access</p>
              <p class="card-label">Partner access</p>
              <p class="card-label gap">Founding partner · 30%</p>
              <p class="card-name">Your brand</p>
            </div>

            <p class="card-role">Trade educator</p>
            <div class="card-qr" data-card-qr aria-hidden="true"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid g3" style="margin-top:40px; padding-top:24px; border-top:1px solid var(--sss-hairline); gap:24px">
        <div>
          <div class="h1 tnum">$0</div>
          <p class="micro faint">What you pay. Ever.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="h1 tnum">30%</div>
          <p class="micro faint">Of all revenue, paid every month</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="h1 tnum">3 systems</div>
          <p class="micro faint">Site, reviews, scheduling — ready to sell</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="page">
      <div class="section-head"><h2 class="h2">You risk nothing here</h2></div>
      <div class="grid g3">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="chip chip--accent" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          <h3 class="h3" style="margin:12px 0 8px">Not a dollar from you</h3>
          <p class="body-sm muted">Demos, builds, hosting, support — every bill is mine. There is no invoice later, and no quota to hit.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="chip chip--accent" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          <h3 class="h3" style="margin:12px 0 8px">Your reputation is protected</h3>
          <p class="body-sm muted">Your name is on the recommendation, so the terms protect it: written service promises, you see my support numbers, and you can pull the plug any time.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="chip chip--accent" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          <h3 class="h3" style="margin:12px 0 8px">Worst case: nobody buys</h3>
          <p class="body-sm muted">Then you've mentioned a useful service once, and I've built a demo for free. You owe me nothing. I only win if your people do.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="systems">
    <div class="page">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 class="h2">Three systems every contractor needs — and pays for monthly</h2>
        <p class="body measure">Not another course. The boring plumbing behind a trade business: the site, the reviews, the calendar. Sold as one stack or one at a time.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid g3">
        <div class="card">
          <p class="label faint" style="margin-bottom:8px">01</p>
          <h3 class="h3" style="margin-bottom:8px">A site that catches every lead</h3>
          <p class="body-sm muted">A clean, fast website for their business — with tracking that catches every visitor: who came, from where, what they looked at, who almost called. Shown to the owner simply, on one screen. No analytics degree needed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <p class="label faint" style="margin-bottom:8px">02</p>
          <h3 class="h3" style="margin-bottom:8px">Reviews & win-back on autopilot</h3>
          <p class="body-sm muted">Every finished job triggers a follow-up that turns happy customers into 5-star reviews. Old customers get caught up automatically: reminders, reschedules, "time for your yearly service". Repeat work without anyone remembering to ask.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <p class="label faint" style="margin-bottom:8px">03</p>
          <h3 class="h3" style="margin-bottom:8px">Scheduling that works 24/7</h3>
          <p class="body-sm muted">Clients who call or write in a messenger get answered and booked around the clock — while the owner is on a roof, in a crawlspace, or asleep. Missed calls stop being missed jobs.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="micro faint" style="margin-top:14px">Prices are set per audience — your people get a partner deal. We agree the numbers together before you mention anything.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="how">
    <div class="page">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 class="h2">How you get paid without doing the work</h2>
        <p class="body measure">Five steps. Your total time: one call and one honest mention.</p>
      </div>

      <% steps = [
        { n: "01", title: "We agree the terms", we_when: "1 call",
          we: ["I show you the three systems, live",
               "We set pricing for your audience together",
               "We sign one page of terms — plain words"],
          you_when: "1 hour", you: "Tell me what your audience struggles with. You already know." },
        { n: "02", title: "I build a demo for your trade", we_when: "1–2 weeks",
          we: ["A sample site + systems for your exact niche — roofing, cleaning, lawn care",
               "Branded so your audience recognises themselves in it",
               "You get a link to show, not a pitch deck"],
          you_when: "0 min", you: "Nothing. React to the demo if you feel like it." },
        { n: "03", title: "You tell your audience", we_when: "Ready when you are",
          we: ["A partner page with your name and your deal on it",
               "I handle every question, demo call and objection"],
          you_when: "1 mention", you: "One video, post or newsletter mention. Your words, no script." },
        { n: "04", title: "I close, build and support every client", we_when: "Ongoing",
          we: ["Sales calls, onboarding, hosting, support tickets — all mine",
               "Written service promises, so your name stays safe"],
          you_when: "0 min", you: "Nothing. Your audience gets taken care of." },
        { n: "05", title: "You get 30% of every invoice", we_when: "Every month",
          we: ["30% of all revenue from clients you brought — setup fees and subscriptions",
               "Paid monthly, for as long as the client stays",
               "You see the payment dashboard itself — not my screenshots"],
          you_when: "0 min", you: "Watch the recurring number grow with every mention." }
      ] %>

      <% steps.each do |step| %>
        <div style="margin-top:20px">
          <div class="row" style="gap:10px; margin-bottom:8px">
            <span class="micro faint tnum"><%= step[:n] %></span>
            <h3 class="h3"><%= step[:title] %></h3>
          </div>
          <div class="grid g2">
            <div class="card" style="padding:16px 18px">
              <div class="row" style="justify-content:space-between; margin-bottom:10px">
                <span class="label">What I do</span>
                <span class="chip"><%= step[:we_when] %></span>
              </div>
              <ul style="margin:0; padding-left:18px">
                <% step[:we].each do |line| %>
                  <li class="body-sm muted" style="margin-bottom:4px"><%= line %></li>
                <% end %>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="card card--sunk" style="padding:16px 18px">
              <div class="row" style="justify-content:space-between; margin-bottom:10px">
                <span class="label">What you do</span>
                <span class="chip"><%= step[:you_when] %></span>
              </div>
              <ul style="margin:0; padding-left:18px">
                <li class="body-sm muted"><%= step[:you] %></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="page">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 class="h2">A sponsorship pays once. A referred client pays every month.</h2>
        <p class="body measure">You know the treadmill: negotiate, post, get paid, start over. A referred contractor keeps paying — and so does your 30%.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid g2">
        <div class="card">
          <p class="label muted" style="margin-bottom:8px">Where the money goes</p>
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table class="dtable">
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td data-label="Split">Your share of all revenue</td>
                  <td class="num">30%</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td data-label="Delivery">Build, hosting, support</td>
                  <td class="num">my 70% covers it</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td data-label="Promotion">The mention to your audience</td>
                  <td class="num">you</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td data-label="Payout">Payout</td>
                  <td class="num">monthly</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td data-label="Duration">For how long</td>
                  <td class="num">as long as the client pays</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <p class="label muted" style="margin-bottom:8px">At $200/mo average per business</p>
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table class="dtable">
              <thead>
                <tr><th>Clients from your audience</th><th class="num">They pay / mo</th><th class="num">You get / mo</th></tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td data-label="Clients">10</td><td class="num">$2,000</td><td class="num paid">$600</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Clients">30</td><td class="num">$6,000</td><td class="num paid">$1,800</td></tr>
                <tr><td data-label="Clients">100</td><td class="num">$20,000</td><td class="num paid">$6,000</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <p class="micro faint" style="margin-top:14px">
            Arithmetic, not a promise — your audience sets the first column.
            But a $1,800 month here repeats next month. A $1,800 sponsorship doesn't.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card card--accent" style="margin-top:16px">
        <h3 class="h3" style="margin-bottom:8px">The end goal</h3>
        <p class="body-sm muted measure">
          Recurring income from recommendations you'd make anyway. Your audience asks
          you "how do I get more customers" every day — now the honest answer also
          pays you, month after month.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="page">
      <div class="section-head"><h2 class="h2">Who am I</h2></div>

      <div class="card">
        <p class="h3">Sergey Yakushevich</p>
        <p class="micro faint" style="margin-top:4px">Senior backend engineer · Batumi, Georgia</p>
        <p class="body-sm muted" style="margin-top:12px; max-width:68ch">
          10 years building backends. 5 of them in payment systems that processed
          350M+ payments. Tracking, follow-ups and scheduling are small systems by
          comparison — the difference is your contractors will actually feel these.
        </p>
        <p class="body-sm muted" style="margin-top:12px; max-width:68ch">
          I got tired of renting my hours to a 9–5, so I ship products alone, start
          to finish — an e-commerce shop with a 3D customizer, an AI integration
          studio, a visitor-tracking platform. All live at
          <a class="link" href="https://cyberjosef.dev/projects">cyberjosef.dev/projects</a>.
          I can build things businesses pay for. What I don't have is your audience's
          trust. That's the deal: my systems, your word.
        </p>
        <div class="row gap-3" style="margin-top:20px">
          <a class="btn btn--outline btn--sm" href="https://cyberjosef.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cyberjosef.dev</a>
          <a class="btn btn--outline btn--sm" href="https://x.com/muffinmanin" target="_blank" rel="noopener">X</a>
          <a class="btn btn--outline btn--sm" href="https://www.instagram.com/sergeyayya_" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Instagram</a>
          <a class="btn btn--outline btn--sm" href="https://github.com/sergey-yakushevich" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="start">
    <div class="page">
      <div class="grid g2" style="align-items:start">
        <div>
          <h2 class="h2" style="margin-bottom:12px">The whole deal on one card</h2>
          <p class="body muted measure">No tiers for you, no invoices, no retainer. I carry the delivery, you carry the trust, and the split never changes.</p>

          <div class="card card--accent" style="margin-top:24px">
            <h3 class="h3" style="margin-bottom:10px">If nobody buys</h3>
            <p class="body-sm muted">You've spent one call and one mention. I've built a demo for free. You owe me nothing. That asymmetry is on purpose — I only win if your audience does.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card" style="border-radius:var(--sss-radius-sheet); padding:28px">
          <p class="label muted">Your share</p>
          <div class="row" style="align-items:baseline; gap:10px; margin:6px 0 4px">
            <span class="tnum" style="font-size:clamp(40px,10vw,52px); font-weight:700; letter-spacing:-0.03em; line-height:1">30%</span>
            <span class="body muted">of all revenue, monthly</span>
          </div>
          <p class="micro faint" style="margin-bottom:22px">setup fees and subscriptions, for as long as clients pay</p>

          <ul style="list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0">
            <% [
              ["You pay $0.", "Demos, builds, hosting, support — all on me."],
              ["One honest mention.", "No script, no post quota, no exclusivity."],
              ["I close and deliver.", "Sales calls, onboarding, tickets — never your problem."],
              ["Terms in writing", "before anything goes live. Either side can walk away."],
              ["You see the real numbers.", "The payment dashboard itself, not screenshots."],
              ["Your clients keep paying you", "even if we part ways later."]
            ].each do |strong, rest| %>
              <li class="body-sm muted" style="padding:10px 0; border-top:1px solid var(--sss-hairline)">
                <strong style="color:var(--sss-ink); font-weight:600"><%= strong %></strong>
                <%= " #{rest}" if rest %>
              </li>
            <% end %>
          </ul>

          <a class="btn btn--primary" style="width:100%; margin-top:24px"
             href="mailto:sergeyayya@gmail.com?subject=<%= u("Trades partnership") %>">Become a partner</a>
          <p class="micro faint" style="text-align:center; margin-top:12px">
            Reply to the message that brought you here, or write to
            <a class="link" href="mailto:sergeyayya@gmail.com">sergeyayya@gmail.com</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="page">
      <div class="section-head"><h2 class="h2">Straight answers</h2></div>
      <% [
        ["What does this cost me?",
         "$0. Your cost is one call and one mention. Every bill — demos, builds, hosting, support — is mine."],
        ["Why would you give away 30%?",
         "Because your recommendation is worth it. Cold outreach to contractors is slow and expensive. One trusted mention from you beats a thousand cold emails — and I'd rather pay you than an ad platform."],
        ["What if my audience has a bad experience?",
         "Your name is on the recommendation, so the terms protect it: written service promises, you see my support numbers, and you can end the partnership any time. Your 30% keeps flowing from clients already signed."],
        ["Do I have to sell?",
         "No. You mention it once, your way. I do the demos, the calls, the closing. If you never mention it again, that's fine."],
        ["What exactly do my people get?",
         "Three systems, together or separately: a site with lead tracking the owner can actually read, automatic review collection and old-customer win-back, and 24/7 scheduling that books the clients who call or message. Working tools, not a course."],
        ["What will it cost my audience?",
         "We set the pricing together before you mention anything, and your people get a partner deal. You'll never be surprised by what your audience is charged."],
        ["How do I know the numbers are real?",
         "You get a login to the payment dashboard — the same screen I see. Every client, every invoice, your 30% next to it."],
        ["What if we stop working together?",
         "The terms cover it: either side can walk away, and you keep earning 30% from every client you brought, for as long as they stay."]
      ].each do |question, answer| %>
        <details>
          <summary>
            <%= question %>
            <span class="faint" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:20px; line-height:1; flex:none">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="body-sm muted"><%= answer %></p>
        </details>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="page" style="text-align:center; padding-top:24px">
      <h2 class="h1" style="margin-bottom:12px">Not sure your audience would buy?</h2>
      <p class="body muted" style="margin:0 auto 24px; max-width:50ch">Send me your channel. I'll look properly and answer honestly — even if the answer is "your people aren't ready for this yet".</p>
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="mailto:sergeyayya@gmail.com?subject=<%= u("Trades partnership") %>">Send your channel</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

<footer class="footer">
  <div class="page">
    <div>
      <span class="wordmark" style="display:block">cyberjosef</span>
      <p class="micro faint" style="margin-top:8px">Sergey Yakushevich · <a class="link" href="https://cyberjosef.dev">cyberjosef.dev</a> · <a class="link" href="mailto:sergeyayya@gmail.com">sergeyayya@gmail.com</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
